# Playground overrides

## Source vs generated

| File | Edit? |
|------|-------|
| `docs/_playground.overrides.json` | Yes — kit-specific source |
| `docs/_playground.json` | No — generated; overwritten |

After edits, from repo root: `yarn generate:docs-metadata`  
Single kit: `cd playbook && yarn generate:playground-configs --kit=<kit_name> --overwrite`

## Authoring rules

- Prefer real prop names in `customProps` / groups (match what developers write).
- Use `requiredProps` for data the kit cannot render without — not only `defaults`.
- Use `structureModes` for alternate JSX shapes; `wrapper` for state/refs/providers.
- Route child/subcomponent props with `propTargets`; use `children.propInjection` for list items.
- For host-only engines (Highcharts, TipTap, MapLibre, …), set `externalDependencies` in overrides — agents in consuming apps must warn, not install.
- Avoid raw `{{ ... }}` object literals inside `template` strings (confused with markers); use a wrapper variable.

Full reference: `docs/PLAYGROUND_CONFIG.md`. Workflow skill: `.cursor/skills/kit-playground/SKILL.md`.
